page('index','Set up Cloak','<h1>Cloak setup guide</h1><p class="lead">Instructions for installing the hardware, calibrating the wrist camera, and running Cloak on an existing DROID system. Select your end effector below.</p><div class="cards">'+cards+'</div>'+section('workflow','The setup sequence','<p>Start with a complete working DROID system. Assemble your end effector, confirm Franka Desk settings, configure the workstation and NUC, calibrate the wrist camera, then run a supervised policy and inspect its mask recording.</p><p>Robotiq can stay mounted when it already follows DROID. UMI reuses its camera mount in a different orientation. Sharpa uses a dedicated bracket and angled adapter.</p>'), [('workflow','Setup sequence')])
page('yam','YAM setup','<p class="eyebrow">Coming soon</p><h1>YAM setup</h1><p class="lead">The full YAM hardware, calibration and deployment guide will be added soon.</p><p>The <a href="stl/droid_camera_closing_part.stl" download>Camera mount - part 1</a> and <a href="stl/cloak_yam_mount.stl" download>Camera mount - part 2</a> are available. The YAM bracket is supplied as received and has mesh irregularities to review before printing. We are validating the end-to-end procedure. Please use the tested Franka guides for Robotiq, UMI and Sharpa in the meantime.</p><p><a href="index.html">Browse available guides →</a></p>',[])
